In a trigger scope, this scopes to all characters with given trait. In an effect scope, this scopes to a random character with the given trait. The given trait needs to have the flag cached = yes. on_hajj = {
    NOR = {
	has_character_flag = hajj_arrived_in_mecca
	opinion = { who = ROOT value >= 0 }
    }
} Warning : count = N doesn't work in this scope, as it's not an any_ scope.

Primarily used to find minor title holders: any_courtier_or_vassal = {
    has_minor_title = title_court_physician
    liege = { character = PREVPREV }
} For direct subjects including courtiers abroad, you must use the inefficient any_character scope instead: any_character = {
    independent = no
    liege = { character = PREVPREV }
}

Scopes to all characters the scoped character has an opinion modifier towards any_opinion_modifier_target = {
    limit = {
	reverse_has_opinion_modifier = {
	    who = PREV
	    modifier = opinion_spying_on
	}
    }
    reverse_remove_opinion = {
	who = PREV
	modifier = opinion_spying_on
    }
}

Scopes to all plotters targeting the specified character, specified by target = some_scope . any_plotter = {
    target = ROOT
    limit = {
	OR = {
	    has_plot = plot_kill_character
	    has_plot = plot_kill_spouse
	}
    }
    character_event = { id = CM.6001 }
}

Scopes to a character who should get a chosen title, from a chosen character's perspective. Parameters: title, perspective (from whose perspective we are viewing the title), index (The index of the character in the list) best_fit_character_for_title = {
    title = PREV 
    perspective = ROOT
    index = 1 
    grant_title = PREV
}

Scopes to all border provinces, including sea provinces when used inside a trigger scope. If bordering sea provinces need to be scoped inside an effect scope, the less efficient any_province or random_province needs to be used instead. Example code that would scope to bordering sea provinces inside an effect scope: random_province = {
	limit = {
		NOT = { province = PREV }
		any_neighbor_province = { province = PREVPREV }
		is_land = no # Include if you only want to scope to sea provinces
	}

	# Do something to this randomly chosen bordering sea province
}
